{"q":"479","t":"Largest Palindrome Product","d":"Hard","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an integer n, return <em>the <strong>largest palindromic integer</strong> that can be represented as the product of two <code>n</code>-digits integers</em>. Since the answer can be very large, return it <strong>modulo</strong> <code>1337</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> n = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> 987\nExplanation: 99 x 91 = 9009, 9009 % 1337 = 987\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> n = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> 9\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 8</code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"largestPalindrome\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"n\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n","g":[{"name":"Math","slug":"math"},{"name":"Enumeration","slug":"enumeration"}],"s":[],"co":[["Google","google"],["Yahoo","yahoo"]],"cs":{"a":[],"b":[],"m":[]}}